    ],
    "notes": [
     "Approximate Yokoo-Pt pressure coverage read from Figure 10, not exact tabulated endpoints. The text reports RP01 to 280 GPa on the lower pressure scale; the Yokoo-Pt reduction reaches about 310 GPa.",
     "Room temperature represented as 300 K; no exact temperature or thermal coefficients are reported.",
     "The approximately 464 GPa Micro16 result is an extrapolation beyond the Re-Pt co-compression fit."
    ]
   },
   "parameter_provenance": {
    "determination_method": "Measurements or their experimental reduction determine this EOS; source: Section 2 (article p. 4), Re-Pt co-compression; Section 3, Figure 10 and following paragraph (article p. 10); Section 4 (article pp. 11-12), V=18.65 A^3 and maximum pressure.",
    "V0": "Section 3, paragraph below Figure 10 (article p. 10; final p. 116): fixed conventional hcp cell volume, 29.47 A^3, Z=2.",
    "K0": "Same paragraph: 358(10) GPa, fitted.",
    "K0_prime": "Same paragraph: 4.8(2), fitted.",
    "temperature_ref": "Ambient-temperature DAC experiment; 300 K is the catalog room-temperature convention, not a measured value."
   },
   "notes": "Published Vinet fit of Re compression on Yokoo et al. (2009) platinum pressure scale. Figure 10 distinguishes conventional-DAC RP01 and ds-DAC Micro17 points; exact fit-row membership and weights are not specified. RP01 used silica glass and a tungsten gasket; Micro17 used glycerin and direct anvil loading. Parenthetical errors are preserved without assuming their confidence level or covariance. V0 is fixed, with no fabricated zero uncertainty. At the rounded reported V=18.65 A^3, the printed parameters give 461.56 GPa versus the reported 464 GPa; the difference is compatible with coefficient rounding. This does not independently refit the original observations. A subsequent Figure 10 vector refit of the 26 RP01 Yokoo-Pt points gives K0=357.19 GPa and K0_prime=4.83483, both within the printed errors. Selecting RP01 and unweighted pressure residuals is a documented reconstruction: adding Micro17 or changing residual coordinates changes the optimum; see the dedicated audit.",
   "pressure_calibration": {
    "status": "partially_resolved",
    "methods": [
     {
      "kind": "equation_of_state",
      "reference": {
       "authors": [
        "Yokoo",
        "Kawai",
        "Nakamura",
        "Kondo"
       ],
       "year": 2009,
       "title": "Ultrahigh-pressure scales for gold and platinum at pressures up to 550 GPa",
       "source": "Physical Review B",
       "doi": "10.1103/PhysRevB.80.104114"
      },
      "source_location": "Section 3, Figure 10 and following paragraph; reference [7]",
      "scope": "Yokoo platinum Vinet scale applied to co-compressed Pt.",
      "notes": "The Dewaele-Pt points in Figure 10 are a comparison, not the pressure scale of this fitted record."
     }
    ],
    "recalculation": {
     "status": "reference_eos_not_bundled",
     "notes": "No exact Yokoo (2009) Pt record is bundled; original paired Pt-Re volumes and pressure uncertainties are also not tabulated."
    },
    "audit_date": "2026-09-10"
